abstract: >
  QISA (Quantum-Inspired System of AI Consensus) is a deterministic,
  multi-perspective reasoning system that converges to stable decisions via
  categorical consensus, adaptive tolerance, coherence metrics, and auditable
  fixpoint verification with hashed traces.
keywords:
  - "AI consensus"
  - "multi-agent reasoning"
  - "categorical methods"
  - "deterministic systems"
  - "auditability"
  - "fixpoint"
  - "convergence"
